WEBVTT

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.800
Y-Yui-chan...

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:12.010
Wh-What do I do?

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:13.780
I'm so nervous...

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.450
The s-song... the sound...

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.570
I've forgotten it all!

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.720
If you can play the beginning,
the rest will follow.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.780
Let's focus on not forgetting the beginning.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.520
O-Okay.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.330
Hey, check her out.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.190
Oh! She's a cutie!

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:35.530
Why are you on the verge of tears?!

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.880
Y-Yui-chan, that hurts!

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.620
The girl with glasses is picking on her.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:39.900
I feel so bad for her.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.980
<i>Honestly! Stupid guys...</i>

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.350
Wow, that's a lot of cheering.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.350
Let's go listen, Yui-chan!

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.990
I've heard enough.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:53.440
Huh?

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.280
Today's the last day I'll be
playing the shamisen, anyway.

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:58.740
The last?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.320
The last time. I only joined the club because
you needed members for this competition.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.080
Oh, right. I see...

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:11.260
Um, then... I'll go take a look
and come back, okay?

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.150
Have fun.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>Today is...</i>

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:21.940
<i>...the last time?</i>

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:29.940
<i>Everything's fine.</i>

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:31.690
<i>I'll do fine.</i>

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:34.490
<i>I can play this.</i>

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:58.510
Those Snow White Notes

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:11.530
<i>Group 13: Touhou Academy Japanese Instruments
Club from Fukuoka Prefecture.</i>

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.540
Episode 8
Tuning Fork

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.000
Ushio!

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.630
Go put on a good show!

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:16.970
Show 'em what you can do!

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.930
That's the boy who stood
out in the crowd, isn't it?

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:22.300
He'll stand out even more
once he starts performing.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.740
They're really good.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:05.360
And fast.

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:08.980
<i>They're good. But...</i>

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:13.900
<i>It's like they're all just ensemble
players supporting that guy's solo.</i>

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:27.160
<i>Arakawa Ushio.</i>

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.330
<i>He's got a wildness and
an originality to him.</i>

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:34.460
<i>If something catches his fancy,
he'll run rampant and follow it to no end.</i>

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:38.460
<i>There it is!</i>

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:43.690
The "Arakawa Twang"!
That's what people call it.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:46.640
It's caused by repeatedly
sliding up and down the strings.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:53.980
<i>Oh, man. This...</i>

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:56.140
<i>...feels amazing!</i>

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:01.860
Arakawa!

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.360
You stick out way too much!

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.460
He really does stand out!

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.570
His personality sure shows in
his performance, huh?

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.520
That was hilarious.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:13.420
If he's like that in the group round,
he'll be a sensation in the individual round!

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:18.830
This jealousy inside my heart just
comes bubbling up to the surface!

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:20.470
I'm all fired-up!

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:23.730
Guys! It's time to go get ready!

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:24.970
Y-Yeah!

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.090
<i>Why's he jealous?</i>

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.010
<i>That one was...</i>

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.140
<i>Yocchan squid jerky.</i>

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:41.100
Okay.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.120
Let's go.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:49.630
Yui-chan?

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:00.140
<i>Yui-chan's nervous, too.</i>

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:03.000
<i>I'm such a terrible person.</i>

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.390
<i>I've only been thinking about myself.</i>

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.260
Yui-chan!

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.550
Don't underestimate this event!

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:18.590
Wh-What on earth happened?

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:20.220
Nothing happened!

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.080
I've just been imbued with fighting spirit!

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:25.800
The guy from Fukuoka's
grandstanding set him off.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:30.850
It's so <i>infuriating</i> how ecstatic he looked,
lapping up all that attention!

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:32.750
It's not about getting attention.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:35.560
We just need to produce a performance
that has a chance of winning.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:36.200
Huh?

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:39.130
What you just said is contradictory.

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:41.970
If we want to stand a chance of
winning, we need to stand out.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:44.840
We <i>already</i> stand a chance!
We have Sawamura!

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:45.520
Yui.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:49.760
I'm only one person. Don't think
we can win just because I'm here.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.480
Now, now.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.770
Let's sing through the piece one last time.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:57.900
All right?

00:06:59.150 --> 00:06:59.890
<i>But...</i>

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.360
<i>The first time I saw Sawamura...</i>

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.990
<i>I felt like he was on a completely
different plane from me.</i>

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:09.260
<i>That's why...</i>

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:11.610
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:13.700
<i>I want to say something to Yui-chan...</i>

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.270
<i>...but I don't know what to say.</i>

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:23.000
Yui-chan, I'm going to give
up on my grandma's song.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.650
Idiot. You can't give up.

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:29.470
I'm certain that Sawamura
will play it for you.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.940
So let's keep trying a little longer.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:35.730
Yui-chan!

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:38.350
Hey! What's got into you all of a sudden?

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:41.690
Why do you always
have to be so strong?!

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:45.010
Show some anxiety for once!

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:47.150
Even if you hate me!

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.660
Oh, isn't that the kid
who moved into our block?

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:02.840
Hey. Wanna play with us?

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:05.760
You don't mind?

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:09.680
Wow! She's so cute!

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:14.010
Yui, look! It's a giant stag beetle.
I caught it at my grandpa's place in Nagano.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.280
Really...

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:19.170
I gotta show it to Shuri, too.
I wonder if she's at home.

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:22.090
I'm sure she is. She doesn't
have any friends, after all.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:24.520
You're her friend, aren't you?

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:27.700
She's weak, so you've gotta protect her.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:29.230
<i>And that same Kaito...</i>

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:32.360
<i>...was the one who made Shuri cry the most.</i>

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:33.950
Yui-chan!

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:35.680
Yui-chan!

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:40.060
Maeda from Class 2's goody
two-shoes act pisses me off.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:43.450
And all the guys are total
idiots for falling for it. Right?

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:44.750
Yamazato.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:48.020
We're ignoring her, got it?
That means you can't talk to her, either.

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:50.090
I'm not doing that.

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:53.080
I hate that kind of mob
mentality with a passion.

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:57.050
Who does she think she is?

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:59.000
<i>Shuri would always walk
alone with her head down.</i>

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:03.170
<i>She wasn't good at talking to people
and would panic mid-conversation.</i>

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:05.830
<i>She never had a bad word to say about anyone.</i>

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:07.580
<i>She was idiotically kind.</i>

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.950
<i>That's just how Shuri is, and I...</i>

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:12.750
I'll keep it going!

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:14.950
Everyone here's joining, after all.

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:17.470
And with Sawamura-kun,
we'll have the strength of a hundred!

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:21.780
<i>I... I...</i>

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.710
I don't hate you!
I'm just angry!

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:30.670
Isn't hating someone and being angry
at them basically the same thing?

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:33.050
No, my anger's directed at <i>me</i>, not Shuri.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:33.760
What?

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:38.650
I just... I keep wondering why I'm like this.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.350
I'm so angry with myself!

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:44.350
Just use that feeling
as your driving force.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.940
Doesn't that solve it?

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:58.720
I... I'm going to play
with everything I've got.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.620
I'm not any good, but I'll work
hard not to make any mistakes.

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:08.590
Still, I'm worried that
I might make mistakes.

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:11.470
What if this mean-spirited, ugly woman
makes a mistake

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:15.840
after how much I've
provoked everyone? Then what?

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:17.550
I just know...

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:23.640
...all of you will blame me, right?

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:26.690
D-Don't be such an idiot.
You're overthinking it.

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:28.230
He's right. You're overthink

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:29.770
I'm <i>not</i> overthinking!

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:33.630
The truth is, I don't want to
go up there in front of people!

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:38.410
But after I've dragged everyone here,
don't tell me I should admit to being nervous!

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:43.450
Yui-chan, you didn't "provoke" anyone.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.360
You gave us all a goal: to win.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:50.060
You've always been the person
I admire the most, Yui-chan.

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:55.370
I know it's past due, but we'll all
help shoulder your worries, okay?

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:58.960
Your words helped me to understand.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:02.410
It's because of everyone here that we
can play without being afraid of mistakes.

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:05.880
Let's do our best! Let's keep trying, okay?

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.730
Let go of me!

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:16.990
No! Let me stay like this for a while!

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:20.640
No! Or that's what I want to say, at least!

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:28.270
Ramune whistle candy.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.450
Matsugorou Cup

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:30.820
Tonkatsu sauce-flavored Umaibou sticks.

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:32.200
Gumballs.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.120
Jumbo Neon jelly snacks.

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:35.480
Yogul.

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:36.880
Sweet kinako chews.

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:38.340
Kneading candy.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:42.020
And the strongest among them is...
Tamago Boro egg biscuits?

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.100
What the heck is this?

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.600
My impressions of the other teams.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.100
These are no help!

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:49.330
Y-You're so cruel!

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:52.230
You're the type of genius who
relies on his instincts, so it's all useless, Brother.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:56.980
Anyway, our rival is this
"Tamago Boro" team. Osaka, right?

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:00.920
The "Yocchan squid jerky,"
Fukuoka, was pretty fun, too.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:01.960
All that's left is...

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:06.400
I was waiting for a friend to perform,
but I don't know when he's on.

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:07.200
A friend?

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:08.990
<i>You</i> have a friend?

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:12.630
We met on a bench outside just
before the opening ceremony.

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:16.010
His team wore samues,
and he was from Aomori.

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:19.500
Maybe he wasn't an entrant after all?

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:20.960
Idiot.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:24.370
That was probably...
Sawamura Setsu, wasn't it?

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:28.680
Oh...

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:30.840
I see.

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.890
So <i>that's</i> Sawamura, huh?

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:39.900
It doesn't seem like he's
been stained by anything yet.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:42.330
Listen closely.

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:46.080
Don't let the sound from the speakers
make you lose track of your own sound.

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:48.970
There will be big speakers
set at an angle behind you,

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:52.360
and the sound coming from them will
probably cause you the most trouble.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:55.770
Before you start, make sure you
imagine how the sound will spread.

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:56.920
How the sound...

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:57.820
...will spread?

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:01.820
If you shrink into yourself,
the sound ends up staying near you.

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:04.320
You want to imagine releasing it!

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:06.940
That way, the sound can
spread in all directions!

00:13:06.940 --> 00:13:08.030
Okay?

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:09.870
O-Okay.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:15.850
1st Annual National High School

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:15.850
Tsugaru Shamisen Koshien

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:15.850
Matsugorou Cup

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:15.850
<i>Group 17. Hokkaido, mixed team: Shivering.</i>

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:19.690
We're up after them.
I'm starting to get super nervous.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:20.910
Really?

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:23.150
You're used to tournaments, Mai.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.860
Mai, the Umezono team's in the
waiting room off to the sideвЂ”

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:27.050
They're finally here?!

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:28.070
Mai?

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:29.980
Wait! We're up next!

00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:33.440
If I don't declare war on Sawamura
before we perform, there's no point!

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:34.940
Sawamu

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:38.360
That's great, everyone!

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:40.590
Your "release poses" look amazing!

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:43.420
A-Are you absolutely sure this is right?

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:46.420
It's wonderful! Feel it in your heart!

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:50.680
<i>That was Hokkaido mixed team, Shivering.</i>

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:52.550
Oh, next up is...

00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:55.470
It's finally time for the
favorites to take the stage.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:04.850
<i>Group 18. Aomori Prefecture,
Aoba Daiichi High School's</i>

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:07.010
<i>Maimai and Her Fantastic Friends.</i>

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:09.480
Okay. Let's go!

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:11.520
What's going on?

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:13.550
It's gotta be Maimai's group!

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:15.400
Shuri! We're gonna go listen!

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:16.250
What?

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.490
Aomori team! You can do it!

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:21.270
Show them that Tohoku spirit!

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:27.180
<i>Sawamura Setsu.</i>

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:30.320
<i>I wanted to battle you one-on-one.</i>

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:46.570
The sound is bursting
open right before our eyes.

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:49.970
<i>Their sound has a nice ring.</i>

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:53.570
<i>The way the sound fills the room is
so different from the other groups.</i>

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:58.670
<i>What I </i>can<i> do right now
is show you my abilities.</i>

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:09.470
<i>That long, long resonance on the top string...</i>

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:11.390
They're singing...

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:15.280
If their top strings weren't
all perfectly in tune,

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:17.950
they wouldn't be able to sing like this.

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:19.440
But...

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:24.540
<i>Strings loosen as you play,
and the tuning will slip slightly.</i>

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:27.200
<i>There's no telling if they'll
stay in tune to the end.</i>

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:33.760
It's split into two parts?

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:37.570
They don't have many members, after all.
Their situation's the same as ours.

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:42.050
I suppose the only difference is that
they're all advanced-level musicians.

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:45.150
"Only" so isn't the word...

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:46.910
That's a really big difference.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:49.930
Don't make jabs at my kind comments.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:54.930
<i>Mai's sound is just too amazing.</i>

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:56.440
<i>I won't let her beat me!</i>

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.380
<i>If I don't dig deep, she'll blow right by me!</i>

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.750
<i>We have to keep up with her!</i>

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:15.410
<i>What's this?</i>

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:19.380
<i>The images the sound is conjuring up
are changing right before my eyes.</i>

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:25.190
This is Tanuma Souichi's little
sister's arrangement, right?

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:26.340
Yeah.

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:31.340
Tanuma Mai's musical expression
is noted for being very modern.

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:32.810
Modern?

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:37.590
Sometimes, it can be seen as a
challenge to the traditional style.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:42.980
<i>It may be a modern interpretation,
but she expresses it well.</i>

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:46.510
<i>It pains me to say it, but it's got her style to it.</i>

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:49.990
Bass, low tones, higher tones...

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:52.320
The three parts are talking to each other...

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.750
They're going all-out.

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:56.750
They're frighteningly good.

00:16:57.920 --> 00:16:59.330
<i>It's true.</i>

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.830
<i>So many different sounds
are flying out... It's scary.</i>

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.100
<i>I won't be beaten!</i>

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:10.510
<i>Who cares about Kousuke and
my brother being amazing?</i>

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:12.470
<i>What does it matter if I'm female?</i>

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:15.850
<i>I am Kamiki Ryuugen's daughter!</i>

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:19.180
<i>Don't underestimate Tanuma Mai!</i>

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:21.890
<i>Mai's running wild!</i>

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:23.390
<i>I can do that much, too!</i>

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:36.700
My ears hurt.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:06.820
<i>That performance stood
out even more than I did!</i>

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:10.080
<i>Just what I'd expect from
Souichi's little sister.</i>

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:12.690
<i>It's such a waste she's not in
the individual competition.</i>

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:14.680
<i>Well, well.</i>

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:17.180
<i>Looks like she wasn't all talk.</i>

00:18:17.180 --> 00:18:18.960
<i>I still don't like her, though.</i>

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:24.700
<i>Sawamura Setsu. What was your
expression when you heard that?</i>

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:27.700
<i>He up and left!</i>

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.010
Are you listening?

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:31.520
Even if you know you can't win,
you can't give up!

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:34.050
As your teacher, I think you're all winners!

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:37.360
Don't act like we're going to lose
before we've even gone out there!

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.100
Well, I mean...

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:43.010
You're up next, but everyone's
motivation has hit rock bottom!

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:40.090
My mind's going blank.
My mind's going blank...

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:44.410
I can't make it
sing like that.
I can't make it
sing like that...

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:44.410
I knew I shouldn't have
listened to other
people's performances.
I knew it, I knew it...

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:48.520
Sawamura-kun, how are you feeling?

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:52.900
Have you lost your motivation after
you heard the team from Aomori?

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:56.030
I said I'd keep up with you all.

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:58.730
My motivation is at its peak.

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:05.160
Setsu and the others are up next, huh?

00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:08.140
I wonder if everyone will be
able to match Setsu's playing.

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:10.630
No. Setsu's going to match them.

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:13.780
He will? You think he'll
come down to their level?

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:15.480
No, that's not what I meant.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:18.720
He hasn't realized it yet, but he's got grit.

00:19:19.030 --> 00:19:23.120
His words and actions come across as
self-centered, so he's easily misunderstood,

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:25.390
but once he decides on something,
he goes at it earnestly.

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:28.230
It's just a shame people don't see it.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:31.350
I feel so much better now.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:34.350
Now that I've heard you
say you're motivated.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:36.890
I see no one trusts me.

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:39.490
Oh, come on now.

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:42.480
It's because we trust you
that we worry so much.

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:43.900
Try to read between the lines.

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:46.060
I see.

00:19:46.890 --> 00:19:47.820
Rai-senpai?

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:49.370
Huh? What is it?

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:53.210
I trust you, too, and there's
something I want to try.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:55.920
After hearing Aomori's
performance earlier,

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.340
I decided I wanted to try
something a little unorthodox.

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.260
K-Kai-chan!

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:07.040
Your mom and dad are here!

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:11.440
You told them about today?

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:13.690
No. They're not interested, anyway.

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:16.550
I'm sure they're just here to
see what it's all about.

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:20.380
You're such a crank.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:26.460
When you hurt your leg and couldn't play
soccer anymore, it was your mother and father

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:28.750
who worried about you the most.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:32.880
Even if he had gone into sports,
there isn't much future in it.

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:37.320
He can just quietly succeed me in my work.

00:20:38.650 --> 00:20:40.120
Huh...

00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:41.760
You think so?

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:44.550
Then they're cranks, too.

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:48.410
The bad blood between me and
my dad isn't going to get better.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:51.470
It's not like it's an easy
problem to fix, after all.

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:53.900
But... well...

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:57.150
I guess I'll let them hear what
we've been up to.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:02.380
You say that like it's super easy.

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:04.770
What if I said it would be difficult?

00:21:04.770 --> 00:21:06.120
I won't let you.

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:07.740
It's going in.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.600
Your skills are sound.

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:12.290
Weave it in.

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:17.210
You really are infuriating.

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:18.040
However!

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:20.130
I don't dislike that sort of thing!

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:23.050
This is starting to get fun!

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:23.920
Is it?

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:31.180
<i>Have Sawamura-kun and Rai-senpai
been discussing things this whole time?</i>

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:37.120
<i>What Yui said earlier was her way of
trying to make me feel better, wasn't it?</i>

00:21:37.610 --> 00:21:39.700
<i>She's quite a crank herself.</i>

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:42.650
<i>She sees into others really clearly,</i>

00:21:43.210 --> 00:21:47.480
<i>but when it comes to herself, she's totally
blind. She's always been like that.</i>

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:51.890
Wh-What is it?

00:21:51.890 --> 00:21:54.570
Huh? Oh, just a thank you for earlier.

00:21:55.030 --> 00:21:57.870
You're kind and you're not ugly.

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:03.070
Th-That was totally uncalled for!

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:05.050
<i>She really isn't used to compliments.</i>

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:11.200
<i>They've finished.</i>

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:14.230
<i>This feels like the
championship game in soccer.</i>

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:17.510
<i>I feel dizzy.</i>

00:22:17.510 --> 00:22:20.560
<i>My heart feels like it's going
to jump out of my mouth.</i>

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:21.690
Well...

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:24.240
Shall we go?

00:22:24.240 --> 00:22:26.770
Why do you look like you're gonna
cry right before we perform?

00:22:29.250 --> 00:22:32.880
Where'd all your usual confidence go?
You've got balls, haven't you?

00:22:32.880 --> 00:22:34.220
No, I don't!

00:22:34.220 --> 00:22:35.620
All right.

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:37.650
From this point on, you need to focus.

00:22:37.650 --> 00:22:40.360
Play the way you always do,
and you'll be fine!

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:45.000
1st Annual National High School

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:45.000
Tsugaru Shamisen Koshien

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:45.000
Matsugorou Cup

00:22:41.100 --> 00:22:44.560
<i>Group 20. Tokyo Metropolis' Umezono Academy.</i>

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:51.330
Well, then.

00:22:52.960 --> 00:22:54.840
Let's go have some fun!
